# Spork 19 turned off, then a clean restart: the teardown stored it, so it loads off (O2b D34)
# and a fork block at a lock's height is no conflict. The tip's INVALIDATE first keeps S2's
# header line from tying with the load (G-T1: the input's own invalidation does not count).
extend main 2
invalidate main@-0
spork off
restart clean
cl main@-0
fork 1 1
